    "created_at": "2022-07-04T18:57:18Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-07-04T18:59:20Z",
    "body": "> We could maybe always buffer events until there's an event listener, similar to workers. (If it's web compatible.)\r\n\r\nThis is a good idea. Currently, the incoming messages are buffered until the event loop is free (as I understand the spec). If you have not attached the listener by then, you miss the events. Buffering until there is an actual listener attached is safer. How to do that without breaking compatibility is a tough question.\r\n\r\n> [In #whatwg Matrix I discussed](https://matrixlogs.bakkot.com/WHATWG/2022-07-04) with @yutakahirano whether there's any delay from the script running in the main thread on opening the network connection, in Chromium, and there shouldn't be.\r\n\r\nUnfortunately this is not what Dev Tools (F12) show. I connect to a websocket very first thing (after <title> tag), yet Dev Tools shows that it starts loading much later, after all other resources. It might be just a bug in Dev Tools (since WebSocket establishes a new TCP connection).\r\n\r\nhttps://www.webpagetest.org/ shows it correctly. So it might be just a bug in Dev Tools after all.\r\n\r\n> You can't do resource hints for everything already even ignoring WebSockets, e.g. you can't preload a form submission.\r\n\r\nRight, but a form submission requires data to send, which client does not yet have. WebSocket and EventSource are much more similar to the GET request.",
