    "created_at": "2022-07-11T02:04:18Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-07-11T02:04:18Z",
    "body": "A page can have any number of connections to the same WebSocket endpoint. Associating the predeclared connections with the ones created by JavaScript seems problematic.\r\n\r\n> We could maybe always buffer events until there's an event listener, similar to workers. (If it's web compatible.)\r\n\r\nThere are people doing every terrible thing you can imagine with WebSockets, including not attaching event listeners. We'd need to have a compelling reason to break those pages.",
